<section id="en" lang="en">
<h1>Privacy Policy – Construction Manager</h1>
<p><small>Last updated: {legal.effectiveDate}</small></p>
<p><strong>Construction Manager</strong> (Vietnamese name: Quản lý công trình, package <code>com.constructionhub.app</code>) is published by <strong>{legal.legalName}</strong>, operating under the <strong>{legal.brandName}</strong> brand. This policy explains what data the app collects, uses and shares.</p>
<h2>1. Data stored on your device</h2><p>Photos, videos, drawings, documents, notes and project details (name, address) are stored <strong>on your device</strong>. We do not read this content unless you choose to share or back it up as described below.</p>
<h2>2. Permissions the app requests</h2><ul><li><strong>Camera:</strong> take photos and record videos of the site.</li><li><strong>Location (precise/approximate):</strong> used only if you turn on the GPS stamp option. Coordinates are printed on the photo and stored with it; they are not sent to us.</li><li><strong>Picking photos, videos and documents:</strong> the app uses the system file picker and <strong>does not request permission to read all your photos or storage</strong>; it only receives the files you choose.</li><li><strong>Internet:</strong> sign-in, shared-project sync, ads, billing.</li></ul>
<h2>3. Google sign-in and account</h2><p>When you sign in with Google (Firebase Authentication) we receive your Google account <strong>email address, display name and profile picture</strong> to identify you and let others invite you to projects. Sign-in is optional if you only use the app locally.</p>
<h2>4. Sharing projects with members</h2><p>When you share a project, the following is sent to Google services (Cloud Firestore): project name, address, member list (emails), notes, captions and file descriptors. Photos, videos and documents of shared projects are <strong>encrypted with AES-256 on your device</strong> before upload to Google Drive; the decryption key of each project is stored in the developer's Cloud Firestore (together with the shared project data). Under the access rules only project members can read this key; however, the developer's system administrators can technically access data on Firestore. The developer commits not to access keys or file contents unless required by law or at your request for support.</p><p>When a member is removed, the key is rotated so that member cannot read new files.</p>
<h2>5. Backup and restore with Google Drive</h2><p>If you use backup/restore or sharing, the app writes files to <strong>your own</strong> Google Drive with limited access (<code>drive.file</code>: only files created by the app). We do not access your other Drive files.</p>
<h2>6. Advertising</h2><p>The app shows ads through <strong>Appodeal</strong> and its partner ad networks. These services may collect your <strong>Advertising ID, IP address, device information and approximate location</strong> to serve and measure ads. You can reset or opt out of ad personalization in Android Settings &gt; Google &gt; Ads. You can remove ads entirely with the Pro plan. See Appodeal's policy: <a href="https://www.appodeal.com/privacy-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer">appodeal.com/privacy-policy</a>.</p>
<h2>7. Payments</h2><p>The Pro plan is billed through <strong>Google Play</strong>. We never receive or store your card or payment details. The app only receives your subscription status (active or not) from Google Play.</p><p><strong>Pro management and device limit.</strong> When you sign in, the app sends to our server (Firebase Firestore) device information: <strong>manufacturer, model, Android version, app version and device identifier (Android ID)</strong>, together with your account name and email. Purpose: to manage Pro entitlement per account, to limit Pro to at most 2 devices at once, and to let the app owner check devices before granting Pro. This information is not used for advertising, is not shared with third parties, and is deleted on request (section 10).</p>
<h2>8. PDF reports and sharing to other apps</h2><p>PDF reports are generated on-device. When you send one via Zalo, Gmail, Messenger, etc., the file is handed to the app you choose and is governed by that app's policy.</p>
<h2>9. Storage, security and retention</h2><ul><li>Data in transit uses encrypted connections (HTTPS).</li><li>Deleted projects stay in the trash for 7 days and are then permanently removed; a PIN protects deletion.</li><li>Shared data on Firestore/Drive is removed when the project owner deletes the project.</li></ul>
<h2>10. Deleting your account and data</h2><p><strong>Delete inside the app:</strong> go to <em>Account</em> &gt; <em>Delete account</em>. The app lists what will be deleted, asks you to type a confirmation word and sign in with Google again, then deletes step by step (you can retry if the connection drops).</p><p><strong>What is deleted:</strong> your sign-in account; projects you own with their photos, videos, drawings, notes, member list and encryption keys (projects with other members are deleted for everyone); invitations you sent or received; your membership in other people's projects; your device list, Pro device seat, Pro grant and profile on our servers. Optional extras: data the app created in your Google Drive (other members lose the photos you uploaded to shared projects) and project data on this device.</p><p><strong>What is kept:</strong> a record linking a Google Play purchase to your account (only an account id and a time) to prevent fraudulent re-use of a subscription. Payment data is held by Google Play under Google's policy. A Pro subscription bought on Google Play is <strong>not cancelled</strong> when you delete your account; cancel it in Google Play &gt; Payments &amp; subscriptions.</p><p><strong>If you no longer have the app:</strong> see the <a href="/delete-account">account deletion request page</a> or email <a href={"mailto:" + legal.supportEmail}>{legal.supportEmail}</a> from the Gmail address you signed in with. We process requests within 30 days. Uninstalling the app removes local data.</p>
<h2>11. "Ask AI" about drawings</h2><p>When you choose to use "Ask AI" in the drawing viewer, the app prepares an image of the <strong>drawing area you are viewing</strong> and hands it to the <strong>ChatGPT (OpenAI)</strong> app on your device, using <strong>your own ChatGPT account</strong>. This happens only after you confirm. Our app does not call any AI service, does not store API keys and does not receive the answer. Once handed to ChatGPT, the data is governed by OpenAI's policy.</p>
<h2>12. DWG to DXF conversion</h2><p>This feature opens a web page outside the app (<code>windfly2909.github.io/dwg2dxf-web</code>, open source) in your browser. The DWG file is converted inside your browser on your device; the page has no upload function and only allows connections to itself (its content security policy). The page is hosted on GitHub Pages, so GitHub may log your IP address when you visit it, under GitHub's policy.</p>
<h2>13. Legal basis and your rights</h2><p>We process personal data under Vietnamese data protection law, including <strong>Law No. 91/2025/QH15 on Personal Data Protection</strong> and <strong>Decree 356/2025/NĐ-CP</strong>, based on your consent when you sign in, invite or accept invitations, and use the features above. You have the rights to be informed, to consent or refuse, to withdraw consent, to access, correct and delete your data, to restrict processing and to object to processing. You can exercise deletion inside the app (section 10); for the other rights, send a request to the contact address in section 16.</p>
<h2>14. Children</h2><p>The app is intended for adults working in construction and is not directed to children under 13; we do not knowingly collect children's data.</p>
<h2>15. Changes</h2><p>We may update this policy; the date at the top shows the latest version. Continued use means you accept the update.</p>
<h2>16. Contact</h2><p><strong>{legal.legalName}</strong> – <strong>{legal.brandName}</strong> brand<br />Address: {legal.legalAddress}<br />Email: <a href={"mailto:" + legal.supportEmail}>{legal.supportEmail}</a></p>
<p><strong>Language notice:</strong> This English translation is provided for convenience. If there is any inconsistency, the Vietnamese version prevails for interpretation in Vietnam.</p>
</section>
